# Googlebook OS on SM-T870: the tablet's sensors multi-HAL with the sensor axes re-expressed for
# the landscape natural orientation (T870-araclar/dogal-yon/hal, yamalar/dogal_yon_hal.py).
#
# It replaces the LineageOS vendor service vendor.sensors-hal-multihal
# (/vendor/etc/init/android.hardware.sensors-service.samsung-multihal.rc). An "override" cannot
# do that from /product: init refuses to override a service "across the treble boundary" (vendor
# and odm files are parsed in the vendor_init subcontext, product files are not;
# system/core/init/service_parser.cpp EndSection). Instead the vendor service is stopped before
# its class starts ("stop" on a service that has not started yet keeps class_start from starting
# it, init/service.cpp StopOrReset) and this one serves ISensors/default in its place, with the
# same class, user, groups, capabilities, task profile and limits.

on early-init
    stop vendor.sensors-hal-multihal

service gbos.sensors-hal-multihal /product/bin/hw/android.hardware.sensors-service.samsung-multihal-gbos
    class hal
    user system
    group system wakelock context_hub input uhid
    task_profiles ServiceCapacityLow
    capabilities BLOCK_SUSPEND
    rlimit rtprio 10 10

# vndservicemanager restarts the whole hal class when it restarts ("onrestart class_restart hal",
# without --only-enabled), which starts the stopped vendor service too. Its registration of
# ISensors/default would replace this one; stop it again and register this one anew.
on property:init.svc.vendor.sensors-hal-multihal=running
    stop vendor.sensors-hal-multihal
    restart gbos.sensors-hal-multihal
